Description: 'NirSoft_RecentFilesView - Nirsoft'
Category: LiveResponse
Author: Dielle De Noon
Version: 1.0
Id: e25ee12d-17f0-4925-94d5-b86e1021aed8
BinaryUrl: https://www.nirsoft.net/utils/recentfilesview.zip
ExportFormat: csv
Processors:
  -
    Executable: RecentFilesView.exe
    CommandLine: /scomma %destinationDirectory%\RecentFilesView.csv
    ExportFormat: csv

# Documentation
# https://www.nirsoft.net/utils/recent_files_view.html
# RecentFilesView lists recently opened/saved files by reading the Recent folder (shell shortcuts to recently accessed files/folders) and the HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\ComDlg32\OpenSaveMRU registry key (recent Open/Save common-dialog history). This is a different artifact from OpenedFilesView (currently-open file handles at run time) already in this repo - RecentFilesView is historical MRU evidence of what a user opened or saved over time, not what's open right now.
# LiveResponse only: verified directly against NirSoft's own documentation - RecentFilesView has no command-line switch for loading an offline/collected Recent folder or registry hive. Its "external source" loading is a GUI-only feature (Advanced Options, F9), not exposed on the command line, so it must be run live against the target system rather than against files KAPE has already collected.
